
Reflection on Mock Interview Experience

-Situation
I participated in a mock interview as part of my work readiness training. 
The interview simulated a real job interview, with questions about my background, skills, and career goals.

-Task
My goal was to perform well in the mock interview by demonstrating confidence, clear communication, and strong problem-solving skills.
I needed to showcase my ability to think on my feet and articulate my value as a potential employee.

-Action
In preparation, I researched common interview questions and practiced my answers using the CAR method. 
I also prepared thoughtful questions to ask the interviewer, showing my interest in the role and the company. 
During the interview, I focused on maintaining eye contact, speaking clearly, and staying calm even when asked challenging questions. 
After the interview, I asked for feedback to identify areas for improvement.

-Result
The mock interview was a valuable learning experience. 
While I cannot see a score for this activity, the feedback I received was overwhelmingly positive. 
My interviewer commended my preparation, my structured answers, and my professionalism. 
I identified a few areas for improvement, such as speaking a bit more slowly, but overall, I felt confident and capable. 
This experience has significantly reduced my anxiety about future real interviews and has given me a clear framework to follow.
